    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d701">

                <pb facs="1099" n="1078" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg1078"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860H.00/6–3048: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Douglas</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret   urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-06-30T22:00:00+01:00">June 30, 1948—10
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2905. For the Secretary and Lovett from Douglas. Bevin<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d701-f1"/> today told me that he had received word from Belgrade
                    that US was considering, against the background of the Cominform action in
                    regard to Yugoslavia, issuing a statement announcing our support for small
                    countries.</p>
                <p>Bevin suggests that we refrain from issuing any such statement until there has
                    been an appreciation of the Cominform action and to have a clearer view of its
                    considerations and significance.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d701-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Douglas</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d701-f1" n="1" xml:id="d701-f1-content">
                <p>Ernest Bevin, British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d701-f2" n="2" xml:id="d701-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 2505, July 1, to London, not printed, replied in part as follows:
                    “Please assure Bevin Dept shares his view desirability withholding statement re
                    Yugo developments pending further clarification and evaluation and has already
                    instructed Emb Belgrade that sense.” (860H.00/6–3048)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
